{
 "phase": "W2b-1: the browser host NTSDWeb draws on the page",
 "change": "native/Sources/NTSDWeb (main, WebSession, WebWindows, WebPage): a wasm32-only executable behind NTSD_WEB=1 with the headless host's services (scripted input only, silent music and sound, no glyphs = the none text group, no sockets, headless geometry with a 3008x1692 screen and a 32-point caption) whose present (and concurrent presenter, the headless pipelined path) calls the wasm import ntsd.present (@_extern(wasm), experimental Extern). The page allocates a SharedArrayBuffer (an Int32 header and 32 MB of pixels); the worker copies each XRGB8888 crop into it under a sequence lock; the page draws the newest frame on each animation frame (a 50 ms interval fallback), swizzled to RGBA, on its own canvas; the first non-black frame drawn is read back from the page canvas and compared with its source pixels; at exit the worker waits up to 5 s for the page to post page.json and the canvas PNG. run_headless_scenarios.py --web fails a scenario without a page report, without a checked frame, with differing canvas pixels, skipped presents, nothing drawn or a page timeout.",
 "design": "The worker never yields while the game runs (its main loop sleeps in Atomics.wait), so a transferred OffscreenCanvas would never reach the page (review round 1); everything between the worker and the page goes through shared memory, which is also how input, audio and message boxes will travel.",
