 "review": "Round 1 (host layer): no result-changing defect; high: a transferred OffscreenCanvas never updates the page while the worker blocks, and the in-worker read-back compared converted bytes (a red/blue swap would pass); low: presentsConcurrently differed from headless, the headless guard was dropped, per-present JS cost. Reworked: page-side drawing through a shared frame buffer, a page-canvas read-back against the source pixels, the headless presentation path, the guard kept until input exists. Round 2: OK; medium: the page report did not gate the row (fixed); low: the seqlock re-check with Atomics.load only acquires (now compareExchange), a torn size could throw (clamped; draw inside the finishing try; the next animation frame scheduled first).",
 "notes": "Linear memory 1.59-1.62 GB as with the headless module. Page draws track presents (rAF fires in headless WebKit too)."
}